#: ../../source/guides/api/conclusion.rst:2
msgid "Conclusion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/api/conclusion.rst:4
msgid ""
"This guide provided an overview of using CodeIgniter4 to build a simple "
"RESTful API for managing books and authors. You learned how to set up a "
"CodeIgniter project, configure a database, create models, and implement "
"API endpoints using controllers and auto-routing, along with the "
"``ResponseTrait`` for consistent API responses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/api/conclusion.rst:6
msgid ""
"From here, you can expand your API by adding more resources, implementing"
" authentication and authorization using `CodeIgniter Shield "
"<https://shield.codeigniter.com/>`__, and exploring advanced features "
"like :doc:`../../libraries/throttler`, "
":doc:`../../incoming/controller_attributes`, and "
":doc:`../../general/caching`. CodeIgniter's flexibility and powerful "
"features make it an excellent choice for building robust APIs."
msgstr ""

